## Project
Use Spring WebFlux reactive style.
Use R2DBC for PostgreSQL.
Use existing Redis connection.

## Database

- PostgreSQL is the source of truth.
- All schema changes must go through Liquibase.
- Never modify database tables manually.
- Create a new Liquibase changeset for every schema change.

## Logging

- Use structured logging.
- Avoid System.out.println.
- Log business events at INFO/DEBUG.
- Log exceptions at ERROR.

## Testing

- Unit tests required for business logic.
- Integration tests for controllers and repositories.
- Maintain high coverage for trading logic.

## Architecture Conventions

- REST endpoints are read/display only and never persist to DB.
- All DB writes happen exclusively through schedulers.
- Service classes must expose two method variants for data that needs persistence:
  - A read method (REST-facing): fetches/calculates, no save
  - A save method (scheduler-facing): calls read method then saves
- Never inject repositories directly into schedulers for writes — all persistence goes through the service layer.

## When Generating Code

- Generate production-ready code.
